course: dictionary
lesson: 1259
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Burnt is a word with a few jobs. It is the past form of the verb burn, so «I burnt my hand» tells you it happened in the past. It can also be an adjective, a describing word, as in «burnt toast». Burned is another correct past form.
explain: Context gives you the clue. «Toast turns brown because sugars and proteins react into new substances; burnt toast is black because it has partly turned into carbon.» Here burnt means cooked too long, so it is black and tastes bad. Check by swapping in your meaning: «cooked too long toast is black» still makes sense.
explain: Burnt can also mean hurt by heat, as in «get burnt». Then it is serious: a burn needs cool running water for many minutes. In the phrase «burnt out», it means very tired. Read the whole sentence before you decide what burnt means.
fact: Burn is a verb. Burnt and burned are both correct past forms of it.
fact: «Burnt» means damaged or destroyed by fire or heat.
fact: «Burnt» can mean cooked too long, so it is black or dark and tastes bad.
fact: «Burnt» can also mean used up as fuel, like wood, coal or calories.
fact: Burning is a chemical change that cannot be undone: burnt paper turns to ash and smoke.
exercise: «Disappointment comes in many shapes: a burnt cake, a band that plays too fast.» What does burnt mean in «a burnt cake»? | *Cooked too long, black and bitter | Cold in the middle | Covered in icing | Very sweet and sticky
exercise: «You can't get burnt when it's cloudy,» says your big sister, and comes home pink. What does get burnt mean here? | Fast asleep | Soaked by the rain | Covered in mud | *Hurt by the sun, going red and sore
exercise: Burnt paper turns to ash and smoke. What does this show about burning? | *It is a change that cannot be undone | It can be reversed by cooling the ash | It makes the paper bigger | It only changes the colour of the paper
test: Ella's dad says, «I burnt my hand on the pan.» What does burnt mean here? | Used up as fuel | *Hurt by heat | Cooked too long | Damaged by water
test: Sam says, «I'm burnt out after the school play.» What does burnt out mean? | Dark and gloomy | *Very tired | Full of energy | Set on fire
exam: «Burnt gases leave through the exhaust pipe, and a catalytic converter changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones.» Which meaning of burnt fits best here? | Cooked too long | Covered in soot | Hurt by heat | *Used up as fuel
